# Board-specific overrides for the source-built RK3576 maskrom usbplug,
# merged on top of configs/rk3576-usbplug.config.
#
# The rkbin prebuilt usbplug (v1.04) has two problems on this board:
#   1. CONFIG_UFS=y makes the plug run UFS link training before serving
#      USB ("Timedout waiting for UIC response" x4, ~20 s), which makes
#      `upgrade_tool db` time out.  The board has no UFS device.
#   2. The SPI NOR is a ZBIT ZB25LQ128 (JEDEC 5e 50 18); without
#      CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_ZBIT the plug reports "unrecognized JEDEC id" and
#      cannot read/write the NOR for maskrom recovery.  The ID entry
#      already exists in drivers/mtd/spi/spi-nor-ids.c (0x5e5018).
# CONFIG_MMC stays enabled: the plug's eMMC probe fails (-95) on this
# board but costs one bounded retry and keeps future options open.
# CONFIG_UFS is not set
# CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_UFS is not set
# CONFIG_CMD_UFS is not set
# CONFIG_SCSI is not set
# CONFIG_DM_SCSI is not set
# CONFIG_CMD_SCSI is not set
CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_ZBIT=y
